<title>USA: Lockheed Martin unit awarded radar contract.</title>
<headline>Lockheed Martin unit awarded radar contract.</headline>
<dateline>OWEGO, N.Y. 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lockheed Martin Federal Systems, a subsidiary of Lockheed Martin Corp, said on Wednesday it was awarded a $12.5 million contract from the U.S. Air Force to upgrade 28 Combat Talon II MC-130H radar sets.</p>
<p>The contract is to make the radars more reliable and easier to maintain.  Radar set modifications will be done for Lockheed by Systems &amp; Electronics Inc of St. Louis.</p>
<p>The contract runs through November 1999.</p>
</text>
